  "details": "<div id=\"parent-fieldname-text-0809c5f5a4ca098d2c1431dcaad5e1f4\">\r\n<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Campochiaro</p>\r\n<p>Activity at the site begins in the seventh and sixth centuries B.C., and the attested sanctuary is built in the fourth century B.C. The sanctuary is situated on two terraces constructed in polygonal masonry. The lower terrace included a long porticoed building with a scenographic aspect.</p>\r\n</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An Italic sanctuary sacred to Hercules located in localit\u00e0 Civitella in the comune of Campochiaro. The site is to be connected with the Pentrian Samnites.",
